Hi Angela,

Thanks for going through the figures with Anthony and me this morning. I've a=
ttached the revised report (BCE-CE-2026-RPT-001-R01) and the separate figure =
register (BCE-CE-2026-TBL-006-R00). The register gives the legend wording, co=
unts, units and report references we checked for all seven figures. Figures 1=
 and 2 use the 30 April pairs, and Figures 3 and 4 use the 24 samples from th=
e July Bennett run.

The Figure 7 caption in =C2=A74.3 now spells out the two label exclusions, on=
e record at 24 h and one at 48 h. The eligible counts are still 12, 11 and 11=
 at 0, 24 and 48 h, respectively. In =C2=A75 I replaced =E2=80=9Cshort-term s=
torage=E2=80=9D with the requirement to document an elapsed storage time of n=
o more than 24 hours, including exactly 24 hours. This limit applies only to =
routine work under the evaluated Bennett nonclinical supernatant measurement =
workflow. The 48 h result remains in =C2=A74.3 as an observed comparison.

Could you mark any comments on the PDF, especially if the Figure 7 caption or=
 the scope of =C2=A75 still needs clarification? I'll keep the April low-band=
 follow-up open as a separate item for us.

Thanks,
Melissa

